```

## Best Practices

### Before Deletion

1. ✅ **Run audit** - Understand current state
2. ✅ **Check references** - Search codebase
3. ✅ **Notify team** - Communicate intent
4. ✅ **Document why** - Record rationale
5. ✅ **Use dry-run** - Preview changes

### During Deletion

1. ✅ **Always use --backup** - Safety first
2. ✅ **Review confirmation** - Read carefully
3. ✅ **Type kind name** - Deliberate action
4. ✅ **Watch for errors** - Monitor output

### After Deletion

1. ✅ **Verify build** - Run go build
2. ✅ **Verify tests** - Run go test
3. ✅ **Update docs** - Remove references
4. ✅ **Commit with context** - Good commit message
5. ✅ **Keep backup** - Don't delete immediately

## Troubleshooting

### Can't Delete: Permission Denied

```bash
# Fix permissions
chmod -R u+w catalog/<provider>/<kind>/

# Retry deletion
@delete-catalog-kind <KindName> --backup
```

### References Blocking Deletion

**Option 1: Fix references first (recommended)**
```bash
# Find all references
grep -r "CloudflareD1Database" catalog/

# Update each reference
# Then delete
```

**Option 2: Force delete (risky)**
```bash
@delete-catalog-kind CloudflareD1Database --force --backup

# Fix build errors after
go build ./catalog/<provider>/<kind>/...  # Shows what broke
# Fix broken imports/references
```

### Accidentally Deleted

```bash
# Restore from backup (if created)
cp -r cloudflared1database-backup-2025-11-13-143022/v1 cloudflared1database/

# Or restore from git
git checkout HEAD~1 -- catalog/cloudflare/cloudflared1database/

# Restore enum entry
git show HEAD~1:shared/catalogkind/catalog_kind.proto | grep -A 5 "CloudflareD1Database"
# Add back to catalog_kind.proto

# Regenerate
make protos
```

## Success Criteria

After deletion:

✅ Kind folder removed
✅ Enum entry removed from registry
✅ No broken references (or documented)
✅ Build succeeds (go build ./catalog/...)
✅ Tests pass (go test -v ./catalog/...)
✅ Backup created (if --backup used)
✅ Deletion report generated
✅ Changes committed

